# The backend image builds from the repository root — it needs `backend/` *and*
# `docs/`, and a context can only have one root. Everything below is either
# rebuilt inside the image, belongs to a different image, or has no business
# leaving the machine.
#
# Only the root context reads this file. `frontend/` builds from its own context
# and keeps its own frontend/.dockerignore. There is no backend/.dockerignore any
# more: it would never be read, because no context is rooted there.
.git/
.gitignore

# The frontend's own image, built from ./frontend. node_modules alone is tens of
# thousands of files and would be sent to the daemon on every backend build.
frontend/

# Docs the UI does not serve are still cheap to copy, so they stay: docs/ goes
# in whole, and `routers/docs.py` decides what is reachable by name.

# Credentials. Nothing below /app is COPYed from these paths, but the context is
# still handed to the daemon whole, and `.gitignore` says the repo-root .env is
# where real endpoint credentials live. The example file is documentation and
# stays.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.log
